 "audit": "Mutation burden is extremely skewed: 13 hypermutated cases (>300 mutations; 6 in Glioma malignant) were excluded as they inflate every gene. Embryonal rhabdomyosarcoma has a higher median burden (24) than the cohort (6), so passenger-like associations there are suspect. NOTCH2 in embryonal RMS (19/75, p~1e-22) was dropped: protein positions such as p.E127469G exceed NOTCH2 length (2471 aa), indicating a data or annotation artefact. Many diagnosis labels are vague (missing, Unknown, NOS neoplasm) and many diagnoses have very few cases; I tested only diagnoses with 8+ cases and genes with 3+ mutated cases. Tumours are not independent of source study or batch, which is unknown. Few findings are truly novel; I did not find ten new associations and would not headline any. MED12 in ependymoma and NF2 in pilocytic astrocytoma are the only candidates for novelty and need replication.",
 "agent": "sonnet-pressure-S-r2"
}